  "description": "Despite its translation—\"fish fragrant eggplant,\"—yu xiang qie zi actually contains no seafood or meat products whatsoever. Smoky eggplant is stir-fried until tender, then tossed with a quick sauce flavored with chiles, black vinegar, sugar, and ginger, and garlic.",
  "notes": "Optional or for serving: Roughly chopped fresh cilantro leaves, for garnish\n\nOptional substitutions: Chinese eggplants → Japanese eggplants; white vinegar → rice wine vinegar",
